// The one image in the program, as its own pixels.
//
// **It is bytes in the source rather than a file in the APK**, which is the same call `sdl3-demo`
// makes: a demo that shipped an asset would be demonstrating that a zip can hold a picture. It also
// keeps the whole program one `sysl build-c` away from an archive, with nothing to package and
// nothing to find at run time.
//
// **A separate module for `bars`' reason** — see that file. A `const` is not module storage and is
// very probably safe beside an `@export`, but the two exports in `main.sysl` are the thing card 0167
// makes vanish, and this is not the file to find out in.
//
// 48x48, RGBA, **eight bits a channel in memory order** — which is `PixelFormat.Abgr8888` and not
// `Rgba8888`. SDL names a packed 32-bit value, so on a little-endian machine the one whose bytes run
// R, G, B, A is the one whose *name* runs the other way. Getting it backwards is a face in the wrong
// colours rather than an error.
//
// The corners are masked transparent, since the picture is a circle and the quad it is drawn on is
// not: 588 of the 2304 pixels have an alpha of zero, and the renderer needs `BlendMode.Blend` for
// that to mean anything.
module face

const SIZE: i32 = 48

// **A `val` rather than a `const`, because a `const` will not take an array literal** — *"the value
// of 'face.PIXELS' is not a constant expression"*. A module `val` whose initializer is constant data
// is laid straight into the object file rather than computed at start-up, which `Exports.storage`
// states outright, so this costs nothing and runs nothing.
